{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 Mr. Barnes introduced the item. He stated that this was the Approval of Amendment No. 2 To Site Access and Construction-Risk License Agreement. \par
\par
Ms. Cohen presented the item. She noted that the Village entered into an agreement with Related to do some pre-closing work on K-Park. Now that they have closed on the east parcel we need to amend the agreement to address the west parcel. She noted that they assigned their interest in that to a related Related entity known as Wellington Property Owners West; which they are allowed to do under the purchase and sale agreement without our approval. She said it reduces the letter of credit they posted for the work to $500,000.00 which is more than enough to cover the work, it allows them to do pre-closing site work on the west school parcel. \par
\par
Vice Mayor Antu\'f1a asked is there anything out of the ordinary that would cause this to be looked at differently.\par
\par
Ms. Cohen answered a question from Vice Mayor Antu\'f1a.\par
}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
